<overview>
<p>The horse remains the most widely used beast mount in human space, carried to hundreds of worlds during humanity's expansion across the stars. Cavalry traditions stretching back thousands of years on Terra have persisted wherever horses thrive, and many planetary militias maintain mounted infantry formations as a practical and affordable supplement to mechanized forces. Horses are fast, responsive to trained riders, and capable of operating across open terrain, grasslands, and light forest without mechanical support. On worlds where industrial infrastructure is limited or where fuel supplies are unreliable, horse-mounted infantry provide commanders with a mobile reserve that requires only fodder and water. These formations excel at reconnaissance, flanking maneuvers, and rapid pursuit, though they remain vulnerable to concentrated firepower and lack the protection of even the lightest armored vehicle.</p><p>Equipped with laser rifles that offer superior range and armor penetration compared to ballistic weapons, these platoons field one of the most effective personal arms available to conventional infantry, though the weapons are significantly more expensive and require soldiers to carry additional power packs.</p>
</overview>

<notes>
Intro date based on prototype date of generic Laser Rifle weapon
